{"content":[{"c":["EZBON"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Gad’s son (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.46.16","r":"Gen.46.16","rawR":"Gen.46.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.46.16","value":"Gen.46.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 46:16"},"), called Ozni in ",{"href":"?bref=Num.26.16","r":"Num.26.16","rawR":"Num.26.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.26.16","value":"Num.26.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Numbers 26:16"},"; perhaps an eponym of a Gadite family."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Benjamin’s grandson (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.7.7","r":"1Chr.7.7","rawR":"1Chr.7.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.7.7","value":"1Chr.7.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 7:7"},"). It has been proposed that ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.7.6-11","r":"1Chr.7.6-11","rawR":"1Chr.7.6-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.7.6-11","value":"1Chr.7.6-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 7:6-11"}," is a genealogy of Zebulun assigned to Benjamin by error, and that Ezbon suggests Ibzan (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.12.8-10","r":"Judg.12.8-10","rawR":"Judg.12.8-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.12.8-10","value":"Judg.12.8-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 12:8-10"},"), a minor judge of Bethlehem."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Ezbon","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 46:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.46.16","rawQueryValue":"Gen.46.16","sourceRefExact":"Gen.46.16"},{"anchorText":"Numbers 26:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.26.16","rawQueryValue":"Num.26.16","sourceRefExact":"Num.26.16"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 7:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.7.7","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.7.7","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.7.7"},{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 7:6-11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.7.6-11","rawQ